## Root causes

1. Netlify has no system FFmpeg in this build image.
2. More importantly, Netlify detected the `next` dependency used by the hybrid build tooling and automatically installed `@netlify/plugin-nextjs`. AccessRevamp publishes the static Vite output in `dist`, so that plugin rejected the otherwise successful build because `dist` is not a Next.js runtime directory.

## Fix

- set `NETLIFY_NEXT_PLUGIN_SKIP=true` for the Netlify build;
- keep the actual deploy target as the static `dist` site plus the existing Netlify Functions;
- pre-optimize all six scrolling MP4 files with the existing scrub-ready H.264 settings and commit the verified outputs;
- keep every clip under the 9.5 MB deployment guardrail;
- preserve strict FFmpeg optimization in GitHub CI and GitHub Pages;
- allow Netlify to verify and publish the already optimized files without requiring system FFmpeg;
- add regression coverage for missing media, oversized media, strict builds, and the Netlify adapter skip.

## Verification

- full Production CI passed;
- a full local `netlify build` reproduction passed without system FFmpeg;
- Netlify Deploy Preview succeeded;
- no UI, routes, payments, pricing, forms, or customer data changed.

