- Fixes #1734

`PeriodicTimer.WaitForNextTickAsync(stoppingToken)` throws `OperationCanceledException` on shutdown. This propagated unhandled out of `ExecuteAsync`, which — given the host's `StopOnUnhandledExceptions` behavior — contributed to restart instability in production.

## Change

Wrap the timer loop in a `try/catch (OperationCanceledException)` so cancellation on stop/restart is treated as a normal exit path, matching the pattern already used inside `RefreshAllStocksAsync`.

```csharp
// Before
while (!stoppingToken.IsCancellationRequested && await timer.WaitForNextTickAsync(stoppingToken))
    await RefreshAllStocksAsync(stoppingToken);

// After
try
{
    while (await timer.WaitForNextTickAsync(stoppingToken))
        await RefreshAllStocksAsync(stoppingToken);
}
catch (OperationCanceledException)
{
    // Normal shutdown -- cancellation during stop/restart is expected.
}
```

Runtime behavior (initial refresh on startup + periodic 30-min cycles) is unchanged.

